      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Proponents argue that vouchers increase competition among schools, allowing students to choose education that best fits their needs and often resulting in improved academic outcomes. Conversely, opponents believe these programs divert critical public funding away from underperforming public schools, exacerbating inequality by primarily benefiting affluent families. The debate centers on whether market-based choice equitably serves students or if it fundamentally undermines the public education system's mission of equal opportunity. Without a local education code review, this sensitive topic requires careful balancing of both perspectives to ensure a fair presentation of facts.",
